# Project LLM — Specification vs Code Audit

> **Specification:** [ProjectFlowExampleProjectLLM.md](file:///e:/onlinewebsites/quiz-platform/ILS_UI_UX/docs/ProjectFlowExampleProjectLLM.md)
>
> **Audit Date:** 2026-10-23

---

## Executive Summary

The **code is approximately 70–75% aligned** with the specification. The core runtime rendering architecture (I1/C1/D1 blocks, TutorialBlockRenderer, UBRC, theme, version routing) is **faithfully implemented and matches the spec**. However, the Project LLM *workflow pages* (create, compliance-brief, external-ai-handoff, candidate-upload, integration-certification) are currently **UI shells** — they display the correct flow visually but are **not yet connected to live backend APIs or real repository discovery**. Several features described in the spec as critical (Engineering Contract generation, candidate verification, runtime/browser verification, certification gate) exist only as planned UI, not working logic.

