## Conclusion

> [!NOTE]
> The specification document is a **design/architecture document**, not a post-implementation audit. It explicitly describes the *intended* architecture and acknowledges that many pieces (Engineering Contract generation, candidate pipeline, verification, certification) are **not yet implemented** and represent future waves (W2–W11).

The **runtime tutorial block architecture** (I1/C1/D1, TutorialBlockRenderer, UBRC, theme system, Composer registry, version routing) is **100% faithful to the spec**.

The **Project LLM workflow** (contract generation, candidate intake, verification, certification) is **designed in the UI but not yet connected to real backend logic**. This is expected — the spec itself frames waves W2–W11 as future implementation work.

**The code is NOT a 100% match to the spec. It is ~70–75% — with all runtime/rendering architecture matching perfectly, and the Project LLM orchestration workflow being the major unimplemented portion.**


