## Answer: **No, it is NOT 100% the same.**

The code matches the specification **approximately 70–75%**. Here's the breakdown:

### ✅ What IS 100% matching (the runtime architecture):

- **TutorialBlockRenderer** — version routing for I1/C1/D1, unsupported version rejection
- **I1** — version router, 9-section canonical locked UI, theme-driven, UBRC identity
- **C1** — canonical code block, theme-driven, UBRC, version validation in renderer
- **D1** — version router, theme validation, UBRC, "single authoritative renderer for ALL brands"
- **UBRC** — all 3 blocks expose `data-block-id/type/version`
- **Brand independence** — no hardcoded SUIA/RTH, theme.primary/secondary only
- **No ILS/LSNB/RSSB inside blocks** — passive participation pattern
- **Composer registry** — `introduction.registry.ts`, `code.registry.ts`, `definition.registry.ts` all exist
- **DomainTheme type system** — complete with semantic color scales

### ❌ What is NOT implemented yet:

- **Engineering Contract generation** (W2) — spec's core deliverable, not built
- **Candidate intake/verification pipeline** (W3–W5) — not built
- **Live repository discovery** — still uses fixture data (spec acknowledges this)
- **Certification gate** (W6) — not built
- **Project LLM workflow pages** exist as UI shells but are NOT connected to real backend APIs

The detailed audit is in the artifact above with line-by-line evidence linking spec claims to actual code files.

